  "summary": "Cold review of src/gpt/liturgy/roman-rite/1962/propers/temporal/68-twenty-fourth-and-last-after-pentecost/main.tex confirms the authorized complete-text mode, the eleven appointments, and two distinct interpretations with four senses each. I compared the revised interpretation with its prior wording and checked selected exact loci in the 1962 Missal and Lasance/Walsh, Augustine\u2019s Psalm 43 \u00a7\u00a78\u20139 and Psalm 129 \u00a7\u00a74\u20135, Chrysostom\u2019s Matthew Homilies 76\u201377 and Colossians Homily 2, Aquinas\u2019s Super Colossenses 1.3, Bede on Mark 11:22\u201323 and 25, Theophylact at Basel fols. 69r\u2013v, and Fromage pp. 503 and 513. At the consequential difficulty, Augustine uses the future praise to read the Gradual\u2019s past rescue as a certain future act, and Chrysostom\u2019s different treatment of \u2018then\u2019 and \u2018immediately\u2019 leaves time between the siege and the final trial. The study explains both inferences and preserves Bellarmine\u2019s alternative. The revised Offertory sentence requires correction against Ritus servandus VII.1\u20135 and 9 (CMAA PDF leaves 60\u201361). Review covered the expansive source and selected controlling witnesses. Its extent excludes a full new collation and inspection of rendered editions."
}
